Table full name: TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_CPTAC_TCGA_PDC_V1_21
Column name: race Type: TEXT Description: An arbitrary classification of a taxonomic group that is a division of a species; the provided values are based on the categories defined by the U.S. Office of Management and Business and used by the U.S. Census Bureau
Column name: ajcc_pathologic_t Type: TEXT Description: Code of pathological T (primary tumor) to define the size or contiguous extension of the primary tumor (T), using staging criteria from the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)
Column name: primary_diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the patient's histologic diagnosis, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O)
Column name: days_to_new_event Type: TEXT Description: Time interval from the date of new tumor event including progression, recurrence and new primary malignancies to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days
Column name: demographic_submitter_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier deriving from data submitter that is attributed to data for the characterization of the patient by means of segmenting the population (e.g., characterization by age, sex, or race) (e.g. P001-DM)
Column name: ajcc_pathologic_n Type: TEXT Description: The codes that represent the stage of cancer based on the nodes present (N stage) according to criteria based on multiple editions of the AJCC's Cancer Staging Manual
Column name: age_at_diagnosis Type: NUMBER Description: Age at the time of diagnosis expressed in number of days since birth
Column name: vital_status Type: TEXT Description: The survival state of the person registered on the protocol
Column name: disease_type Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the type of malignant disease, as categorized by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O)
Column name: days_to_last_follow_up Type: NUMBER Description: Time interval from the date of last follow up to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days
Column name: diagnosis_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier for data from the investigation, analysis and recognition of the presence and nature of disease, condition, or injury from expressed signs and symptoms; also, the scientific determination of any kind; the concise results of such an investigation (e.g. e8dd475b-693a-11ea-b1fd-0aad30af8a83)
Column name: days_to_last_known_disease_status Type: NUMBER Description: Time interval from the date of last follow up to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days
Column name: ajcc_pathologic_stage Type: TEXT Description: The extent of a cancer, especially whether the disease has spread from the original site to other parts of the body based on AJCC staging criteria
Column name: demographic_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier attributed to data for the characterization of the patient by means of segmenting the population--for instance, characterization by age, sex, or race (e.g. 848b480c-0f56-11e9-a064-0a9c39d33490)
Column name: gender Type: TEXT Description: Text designations that identify gender; identification is self-reported and may come from a form, questionnaire, interview, etc.
Column name: ethnicity Type: TEXT Description: An individual's self-described social and cultural grouping, specifically whether an individual describes themselves as Hispanic or Latino, based on the categories defined by the U.S. Office of Management and Business and used by the U.S. Census Bureau
Column name: case_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier associated with a specific patient (e.g. 24cb0fcb-63d6-11e8-bcf1-0a2705229b82)
Column name: primary_site Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the general location of the malignant disease, as categorized by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O)
Column name: tumor_stage Type: TEXT Description: The extent of a cancer in the body. Staging is usually based on the size of the tumor, whether lymph nodes contain cancer, and whether the cancer has spread from the original site to other parts of the body. The accepted values for tumor_stage depend on the tumor site, type, and accepted staging system. These items should accompany the tumor_stage value as associated metadata
Column name: diagnosis_submitter_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier deriving from data submitter attributed to data from the investigation, analysis and recognition of the presence and nature of disease, condition, or injury from expressed signs and symptoms; also, the scientific determination of any kind; the concise results of such an investigation (e.g. 33-DX)
Column name: site_of_resection_or_biopsy Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of origin, of the patient's malignant disease, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O)
Column name: ajcc_pathologic_m Type: TEXT Description: Code to represent the defined absence or presence of distant spread or metastases (M) to locations via vascular channels or lymphatics beyond the regional lymph nodes, using criteria established by the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)
Column name: case_submitter_id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier deriving from the data submitter that is associated with a specific patient (e.g. 05BR016)
