Table full name: TCGA.TCGA_VERSIONED.CLINICAL_GDC_R37
Column name: proj__project_id Type: TEXT Description: GDC-assigned identifier for the project to which a case belongs.
Column name: diag__ajcc_pathologic_stage Type: TEXT Description: The extent of a cancer, especially whether the disease has spread from the original site to other parts of the body based on AJCC staging criteria.
Column name: demo__days_to_birth Type: NUMBER Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date from a person's date of birth represented as a calculated negative number of days.
Column name: diag__year_of_diagnosis Type: NUMBER Description: Numeric value to represent the year of an individual's initial pathologic diagnosis of cancer.
Column name: demo__gender Type: TEXT Description: Text designations that identify gender. Gender is described as the assemblage of properties that distinguish people on the basis of their societal roles. [Explanatory Comment 1: Identification of gender is based upon self-report and may come from a form, questionnaire, interview, etc.]
Column name: disease_type Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the type of malignant disease, as categorized by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: primary_site Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the primary site of disease, as categorized by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O). This categorization groups cases into general categories. Reference tissue_or_organ_of_origin on the diagnosis node for more specific primary sites of disease.
Column name: diag__primary_diagnosis Type: TEXT Description: Text term used to describe the patient's histologic diagnosis, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: demo__ethnicity Type: TEXT Description: An individual's self-described social and cultural grouping, specifically whether an individual describes themselves as Hispanic or Latino. The provided values are based on the categories defined by the U.S. Office of Management and Business and used by the U.S. Census Bureau.
Column name: diag__tissue_or_organ_of_origin Type: TEXT Description: The text term used to describe the anatomic site of origin, of the patient's malignant disease, as described by the World Health Organization's (WHO) International Classification of Diseases for Oncology (ICD-O).
Column name: demo__days_to_death Type: NUMBER Description: Number of days between the date used for index and the date from a person's date of death represented as a calculated number of days.
Column name: diag__last_known_disease_status Type: TEXT Description: Text term that describes the last known state or condition of an individual's neoplasm.
Column name: demo__vital_status Type: TEXT Description: The survival state of the person registered on the protocol.
Column name: demo__age_at_index Type: NUMBER Description: The patient's age (in years) on the reference or anchor date date used during date obfuscation.
Column name: diag__progression_or_recurrence Type: TEXT Description: Yes/No/Unknown indicator to identify whether a patient has had a new tumor event after initial treatment.
Column name: demo__race Type: TEXT Description: An arbitrary classification of a taxonomic group that is a division of a species. It usually arises as a consequence of geographical isolation within a species and is characterized by shared heredity, physical attributes and behavior, and in the case of humans, by common history, nationality, or geographic distribution. The provided values are based on the categories defined by the U.S. Office of Management and Business and used by the U.S. Census Bureau.
Column name: diag__ajcc_clinical_stage Type: TEXT Description: Stage group determined from clinical information on the tumor (T), regional node (N) and metastases (M) and by grouping cases with similar prognosis for cancer.
